  "_schema": "The biggest single mass in most builds, and the only source of voltage sag. 'cells' sets pack voltage, which sets the RPM ceiling (max_RPM = KV * live voltage) — this is most of why a 4S->6S swap feels dramatic rather than cosmetic. 'internal_r_ohm' is what makes that voltage live rather than fixed: punch the throttle, current spikes, voltage drops, RPM ceiling drops, thrust drops. The Li-ion entry exists specifically to expose that mechanism.",
